{
  "name": "a-space-keeps-its-tint-after-a-cross-profile-switch",
  "description": "Personal and New Space are on the Default profile, BPX on Profile 1. New Space and BPX wear Nocturne themes with different stop positions (maroon top-left on New Space, right-middle on BPX). Page tint is on. New Space must look the same whether the switch into it starts from Personal or from BPX. The recorded bug: from BPX it lands, then shows BPX's theme and tint and stays there. A swipe from BPX stages the scrub on the Profile 1 controller, the switch hands the window to Default, and the scrub's end is routed to Default, so the New Space theme is never promoted. The keyboard bounces after it check that a sampler frame from BPX's page does not land as a glow after the switch cleared it.",
